# Go style

Follow [docs/go.md](docs/go.md): [Effective Go](docs/go/effective.md), [doc comments](docs/go/comment.md), then [code review comments](docs/go/review.md).

Repo overrides (win over those guides):

- Filenames: lowercase, no separators, one word when possible.
- No `failed to` prefix on logs or errors.
- Wrap with `fmt.Errorf("...: %w", err)` inside repo and other non-HTTP Go, not `pkg/errors`. Do not wrap `srvcerror.E` in `%w` before HTTP. See [docs/errors.md](docs/errors.md).
- No Makefile for fmt/vet/test unless we add one on purpose.
- Keep `cmd/` `modules/` `common/` `postgres/`. Do not adopt golang-standards/project-layout.
- Do not add new `util` / `misc` / `types` packages.

`gofmt` every Go file. `go vet ./...` before commit.
